  "reason": "Evidence: The top 4 experiments all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, with transformer+weighted (config_043, 0.725) as the best. We've fully explored that 2x2 aggregation×fusion space. The only untested scvi_n200 multimodal direction is with resnet50 (only avgpool+weighted was tested at 0.678). Question: Does transformer aggregation provide the same ~1-2% boost with resnet50 that it did with ViT? This tests whether the aggregation benefit is encoder-agnostic or specific to ViT's patch structure. Why this is the best use: With only 2 experiments remaining, this is the most logical exploitation step — it extends our strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted) to the one untested image encoder, clarifying whether the architecture is robust or whether ViT is essential. If it approaches 0.70+, it confirms we're near the ceiling for this model family; if it lags significantly, it reinforces that imagenet_vit_l is critical and we should accept config_043 as the likely optimum."
}

